{"text": "Slide 1\nEstate of Philomena Guarnieri v. Heron Pointe Care Center\nMediation before Hon. Leland Mabry (Ret.) — November 19, 2025\nCivil Action No. STCV24-01187, State Court of Chatham County\nFarrier Nettles Trial Group for the plaintiffs — CONFIDENTIAL SETTLEMENT COMMUNICATION\nSpeaker notes: Open with the photograph of Mrs. Guarnieri at her 95th birthday. Do not show the wound photos until slide 4. Rosemarie will step out for that slide.\n\nSlide 2\nWho she was\nBorn December 8, 1927 in Savannah; seamstress for 40 years; widow; two children\nAdmitted to Heron Pointe on March 3, 2023, walking with a walker, mild dementia, weight 131 lb\nDied January 22, 2024, age 96\nSpeaker notes: She attended Mass daily at the cathedral until she was 93. The defense will say she was 96 and frail. Our answer: she was 96 and walking when she arrived.\n\nSlide 3\nTimeline of the wound\nDate\tRecord\tEvent\n10/02/23\tBraden Scale\tScored high risk; no care plan change\n11/14/23\tNurse note\t\"Redness to sacrum\" — no physician notified\n12/19/23\tWound nurse\tStage 3 sacral pressure ulcer, first measurement\n1/9/24\tHospital ED\tStage 4 ulcer to bone, osteomyelitis, sepsis; weight 104 lb\n1/22/24\tHospice\tDeath\nSpeaker notes: Turning logs for December are blank on 41 of 93 shifts. Two aides will testify the unit ran one aide to 22 residents on nights. One of them, the night aide who was fired after she called the state hotline, is our best witness and is afraid of losing her new job.\n\nSlide 4\nLiability\nState survey of 2/6/2024 (CMS Form 2567): deficiency under 42 CFR § 483.25, F-tag 686, \"actual harm\"\nDr. Shirin Vossoughi, geriatrician: the ulcer was avoidable; 27 lb weight loss in ten weeks went unaddressed\nCorporate parent Altamaha Senior Holdings, LLC cut the nursing budget $310,000 in 2023\n\nSlide 5\nDamages\nMedical expenses: $187,442.19 (Medicare lien $61,208.33)\nFuneral: $11,950\nPain and suffering, ten weeks; full value of the life under O.C.G.A. § 51-4-2\nOpening demand: $2,750,000\nSpeaker notes: Authority from the clients: do not go below $900,000 without calling them. Rosemarie Guarnieri-Platt is the administrator and decides. Her brother Dominic Guarnieri wants to try the case; he has not spoken to her since the funeral and will attend by video from Jacksonville. Carrier is Coastal Empire Assurance, policy CEA-LTC-0044187, limits $1,000,000 per claim, eroding. Defense costs to date are probably $140K, so real money available is about $860,000.\n\nSlide 6\nLogistics\nPlaintiffs' room: conference room B; Odell Farrier lead, cell 912-555-0141\nRosemarie: 912.555.0189, rgplatt@moonrivermail.example\nProposed payee if settled: the estate account ending 4418; probate no. E-2024-0612\nSpeaker notes: Dominic filed for Chapter 7 last year. His share may belong to his trustee. Raise it with the mediator privately, not in the joint session.", "kind": "PowerPoint presentation", "detail": "6 slides · 457 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Philomena Guarnieri", "Rosemarie", "Shirin Vossoughi", "Rosemarie Guarnieri-Platt", "Dominic Guarnieri", "Odell Farrier"], "companies": ["Heron Pointe Care Center", "Savannah", "Altamaha Senior Holdings", "CMS", "Coastal Empire Assurance"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Jacksonville"], "health": ["dementia", "weight loss"], "sensitive": ["race or ethnicity", "religion", "political views or donations", "criminal history"], "names": ["Philomena", "Rosemarie", "Shirin", "Dominic", "Odell"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 2.7999999970197678, "modelMs": 27090.70000000298, "topicMs": 30459.10000000149, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 18, "end": 37, "text": "Philom